{"name":"Elf Slippers","hex":"#a6a865","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being or spirit associated with illness, mischief, and harmful or dangerous magical influence; in later Norse sources, sometimes divided into benevolent light elves (inhabiting  Álfheimr) and malevolent dark elves.","A small, magical creature similar to a fairy, often mischievous, playful, or occasionally helpful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist into elflocks (of hair); to mat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elf"},{"term":"slippers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of slipper"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of slipper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slippers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elf","blocks":[{"text":"An elf is a type of humanoid supernatural being in Germanic folklore. Elves appear especially in North Germanic mythology, being mentioned in the Icelandic Poetic Edda and the Prose Edda."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg/330px-%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elf"},{"title":"Slipper","blocks":[{"text":"Slippers are a type of shoes falling under the broader category of light footwear, that are easy to put on and off and are intended to be worn indoors, particularly at home. They provide comfort and protection for the feet when walking indoors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Slippers.jpg/330px-Slippers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slipper"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.p